## 9. Canonical Types

### 9.1 Primitive identifiers

```rust
pub struct ChainId(pub [u8; 32]);
pub struct ActorId(pub Ed25519PublicKey);
pub struct JobId(pub Sha256Digest);
pub struct ClaimId(pub Sha256Digest);
pub struct AttestationId(pub Sha256Digest);
pub struct EvidenceId(pub Sha256Digest);
pub struct ChallengeId(pub Sha256Digest);
pub struct CommitmentId(pub Sha256Digest);
pub struct ActionId(pub Sha256Digest);
pub struct MechanismSetId(pub Sha256Digest);
pub struct ExperimentId(pub Sha256Digest);
```

Identifiers are derived from canonical encoded content with domain-separated SHA-256 hashing.

### 9.2 Domain separation

At minimum:

```text
validation-network/action/v1
validation-network/job/v1
validation-network/claim/v1
validation-network/evidence/v1
validation-network/commitment/v1
validation-network/block/v1
validation-network/state/v1
validation-network/mechanism-set/v1
validation-network/experiment/v1
```

The signing domain MUST include:

* protocol version;
* chain ID;
* object class;
* canonical payload.

### 9.3 Bounded data

Every consensus-decoded variable-length value MUST have an explicit maximum.

Initial bounds:

```text
repository locator       512 bytes
content locator hint     512 bytes
claim statement          4 KiB
counterclaim              4 KiB
metadata                  8 KiB
action                    64 KiB
evidence manifest ref     2 KiB
actions per block         1,024
block body                4 MiB
claims per job            128
attestations per claim    1,024
open challenges per claim 256
```

These are protocol parameters and become part of the genesis configuration.

### 9.4 No floating point

Consensus state and economic calculations MUST NOT use floating-point values.

Use:

* integer counts;
* basis points;
* explicitly scaled signed integers;
* checked arithmetic;
* declared rounding rules.

Overflow checks MUST remain enabled in development, test, and release profiles.

