## 10. Git Artifact Model

```rust
pub enum GitHash {
    Sha1([u8; 20]),
    Sha256([u8; 32]),
}

pub struct ContentRef {
    pub digest: Sha256Digest,
    pub locator_hint: BoundedBytes<512>,
    pub media_type: BoundedBytes<128>,
}

pub struct GitArtifact {
    pub repository: BoundedBytes<512>,
    pub base_commit: GitHash,
    pub candidate_commit: GitHash,
    pub specification: ContentRef,
}
```

The repository locator is informational and used by operators.

The immutable identity of the software change is:

```text
repository locator
+ base commit
+ candidate commit
+ specification digest
```

A changed candidate commit or specification produces a new job.

A revised job MAY reference its predecessor through:

```rust
pub supersedes: Option<JobId>
```

