## 20. Action Ingress and Pending Pool

The consensus protocol does not define customer-facing action submission. The node therefore includes a small ingress subsystem.

### 20.1 External ingress

Initial RPC:

```text
POST /v1/actions
GET  /v1/actions/{action_id}
GET  /v1/jobs
GET  /v1/jobs/{job_id}
GET  /v1/actors/{actor_id}
GET  /v1/blocks/{height}
GET  /v1/state/root
GET  /v1/health
```

RPC JSON is not consensus encoding.

The node decodes JSON, constructs or accepts canonical action bytes, verifies the signature, and inserts the canonical action into the pending pool.

### 20.2 Peer forwarding

A valid action received by one consensus node is forwarded over an authenticated action channel to the other committee nodes.

### 20.3 Pending pool

The pending pool is bounded and deduplicated by `ActionId`.

Required limits:

* maximum actions globally;
* maximum actions per actor;
* maximum total bytes;
* maximum nonce gap;
* expiry by `valid_until_height`.

Candidate selection is deterministic from the proposer’s current pool:

```text
(actor_id, nonce, action_id)
```

This ordering is not an economic fairness policy. It is a simple reproducible v1 rule.

Fee markets, priority auctions, and public mempool policy are deferred.

