## 21. Encoding and Conformance

All consensus objects implement `commonware_codec` traits directly.

Do not use:

* `bincode`;
* default `serde_json`;
* architecture-dependent memory layouts;
* unbounded decoding;
* undocumented enum discriminants.

Every public consensus type must have:

* explicit discriminants;
* explicit maximum lengths;
* test vectors;
* round-trip tests;
* malformed-input tests;
* truncation tests;
* trailing-byte tests;
* stable conformance hashes.

`commonware_conformance` should lock mechanism and encoding outputs into checked-in TOML vectors so accidental serialization changes fail CI.

A codec change requires:

* `CodecVersion` increment;
* migration or new genesis;
* conformance vector update with explicit review;
* replay of all retained exploit traces.

