## 22. Mechanism Architecture

Economic modules are compiled, deterministic policy components.

They are not:

* dynamic native plugins;
* WASM smart contracts;
* downloaded capabilities;
* arbitrary user-supplied code.

This is deliberate. Runtime plugin systems would enlarge the consensus and security surface before the economic model exists.

### 22.1 Mechanism manifest

```rust
pub struct MechanismManifest {
    pub id: MechanismId,
    pub version: MechanismVersion,
    pub status: MechanismStatus,
    pub requires: BoundedVec<MechanismId, 16>,
    pub reads_exports: BoundedVec<MechanismExportId, 32>,
    pub state_namespace: MechanismNamespace,
    pub config_digest: Sha256Digest,
}

pub enum MechanismStatus {
    Proposed,
    Implemented,
    Experimental,
    Accepted,
    Rejected,
    Superseded,
}
```

### 22.2 Mechanism interface

```rust
pub trait Mechanism {
    fn manifest(&self) -> MechanismManifest;

    fn validate_config(
        &self,
        config: &[u8],
    ) -> Result<(), MechanismError>;

    fn pre_action(
        &self,
        view: &MechanismReadView<'_>,
        action: &SignedAction,
    ) -> Result<(), MechanismError>;

    fn on_event(
        &self,
        view: &MechanismReadView<'_>,
        event: &CanonicalEvent,
    ) -> Result<Vec<MechanismMutation>, MechanismError>;

    fn on_epoch(
        &self,
        view: &MechanismReadView<'_>,
        epoch: u64,
    ) -> Result<Vec<MechanismMutation>, MechanismError>;

    fn check_invariants(
        &self,
        view: &MechanismReadView<'_>,
    ) -> Result<(), MechanismInvariantError>;
}
```

### 22.3 Compiled registry

A concrete enum wraps every implemented mechanism:

```rust
pub enum MechanismInstance {
    M00RecordOnly(M00Config),
    M01NaiveReputation(M01Config),

    // Added only after their implementation experiments begin.
}
```

The mechanism set is an ordered list of implemented instances.

Selection of a catalog entry with `Proposed` status is a configuration error.

### 22.4 Dependencies

A mechanism may read only:

* canonical state;
* its own state;
* exports of mechanisms listed in `requires`.

The mechanism registry topologically sorts dependencies at genesis.

Cycles invalidate the mechanism set.

### 22.5 State isolation

Each mechanism writes only beneath:

```text
30/mechanism/<module-id>/<version>/...
```

Cross-module writes are forbidden.

### 22.6 Mutation order

For each canonical event:

1. All modules read the same finalized pre-event view plus declared dependency exports.
2. Modules emit mutations.
3. Mutations are sorted by mechanism ID and key.
4. Namespace collisions invalidate execution.
5. Mutations are applied.
6. Module invariants run.

A module does not observe another module’s same-event mutation unless that interaction is represented through a separately specified processing phase.

Do not create hidden order dependencies.

