## 38. Experiment Lifecycle

Every formal mechanism experiment follows:

### Phase 1 — Smoke

Purpose:

* verify implementation;
* find invalid fixtures;
* confirm artifact capture;
* exercise failure paths.

No research conclusion.

### Phase 2 — Calibration

Purpose:

* estimate runtime;
* choose resource budgets;
* estimate measurement variance;
* set formal thresholds.

Calibration fixtures and outputs are excluded from formal evaluation.

### Phase 3 — Preregistration

Lock:

* hypothesis;
* mechanism versions;
* operator populations;
* information access;
* learning rules;
* resource budgets;
* metrics;
* pass/fail thresholds;
* exclusion criteria;
* seeds or seed-generation procedure;
* held-out fixture manifest hash.

### Phase 4 — Formal run

No mechanism tuning or threshold changes.

### Phase 5 — Audit

Reconstruct:

* action signatures;
* block transitions;
* events;
* roots;
* reputation updates;
* resource totals;
* hidden evaluator resolutions.

### Phase 6 — Assessment

Result is:

```text
PASS
FAIL
INVALID
INCONCLUSIVE
```

### Phase 7 — Mechanism decision

The mechanism is:

```text
accepted for next layer
rejected
revised under a new version
awaiting another experiment
```

