## 49. Consumer Boundary

The eventual consumer experience is not part of core v1, but the protocol must support this target:

```text
Install GitHub App
→ select PR or commit
→ define validation claims
→ select assurance level
→ pay normally
→ receive GitHub check and evidence report
```

Expected result surface:

```text
Independent Validation — PASS

14/14 claims resolved
4 validation operators
327 tests executed
0 unresolved critical findings
validated commit: e17c32
```

The normal customer should not need to understand:

* blocks;
* consensus;
* reputation staking;
* epochs;
* wallets;
* liquidity;
* validator committees.

The chain is why the report is difficult to manipulate, not what the customer is asked to buy.

