# 53. Agent Execution Rules

The implementation agent MUST:

1. Work only on the current milestone and its dependencies.
2. Treat this specification as authoritative unless a documented Commonware API mismatch makes a requirement impossible.
3. Record API mismatches in `docs/commonware-spike.md`.
4. Create an issue before materially changing a fixed v1 decision.
5. Preserve old mechanism behavior and experiment artifacts.
6. Add tests before marking a work item complete.
7. Use real Commonware components for release-path integration.
8. Keep consensus logic free of model, Git, shell, and web calls.
9. Keep consensus-node and validation-operator identities separate.
10. Stop adding abstractions when the current milestone can be satisfied without them.
11. Not implement UI, tokens, registries, dynamic plugins, governance, or M02–M12.
12. Produce machine-readable output for every CLI command intended for agents.
13. Record assumptions, decisions, validation evidence, and failed attempts through the project’s provenance workflow.
14. Never silently weaken an acceptance gate to complete a ticket.

A milestone is complete only when its stated gate has been executed and its evidence retained.

---

# 54. Definition of Core v1 Complete

Core v1 is complete when all of the following are true:

* A four-node Commonware network finalizes validation blocks.
* The network uses real authenticated P2P, buffered broadcast, Simplex, marshal, Stateful, and QMDB components.
* Nodes independently reproduce identical receipts and state roots.
* A restarted node recovers without manual state repair.
* Git-backed jobs, claims, evidence references, attestations, and experimental resolutions work end to end.
* M00 and M01 are selectable by genesis configuration.
* M02–M12 exist only as catalog proposals.
* Scripted and autonomous operators can submit signed actions.
* Closed-loop agent decisions are captured and exactly replayable as action traces.
* H-REP-001 has a preregistered formal result.
* At least one non-productive reputation strategy has been captured as a permanent exploit artifact.
* The exploit has produced a new hypothesis or an evidence-backed decision that no new mechanism is yet justified.
* The repository can explain every implemented economic rule through its experimental lineage.

The project should not claim that it has solved validation economics at this point.

It should be able to make a narrower and stronger claim:

> We built a functioning validation blockchain, deployed autonomous agents as economic operators, measured how they exploited its first reputation mechanism, and preserved the resulting evidence as the basis for the next design layer.
